{
  "claims": [
    "In the area of Borgocarbonara and Magnacavallo, the adherence rate to telemonitoring for patients living alone more than 40 km away is 0.0%, involving 5 patients, while in the rest of the ATS it is 87.69%.",
    "In the commune of Borgocarbonara, the telemonitoring adherence rate is 57.14% among 7 patients, while in Poggio Rusco it is 54.-55% among 11 patients; in both cases, the rates are significantly below the ATS average (83.08%).",
    "There are 150 patients with delayed telemonitoring, with a maximum delay of 98 days; the patients with the greatest delay have a risk score ranging from 0.0211 to 0.0596.",
    "In the ASST Mantova, the telemonitoring adherence rate is 66.1%, while for cardiology visits it is 75.14%, for echocardiography it is 74.32%, and for BNP test it is 93.87%."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The main problem is concentrated in the area of Borgocarbonara and Magnacavallo, where telemonitoring adherence is zero. Even in nearby communes such as Poggio Rusco and Sermide e Felonica, the rates are very low. Delay in telemonitoring is widespread, involving 150 patients, and the ASST Mantova has a telemonitoring adherence rate below the ATS average. The intervention must focus on Borgocarbonara and Magnacavallo, with targeted actions to restore telemonitoring adherence, particularly for high-risk and delayed patients."
}
